1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,113
This American town can only be reached by land through Canada.

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:12,187
In 1846, Britain and the United States drew their border along the 49th parallel.

3
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:17,714
But one small peninsula south of Vancouver dips just below that line.

4
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:20,268
So its tip became American.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,670
Today, people in Point Roberts, Washington cross two international borders

6
00:00:25,670 --> 00:00:29,038
just to drive to the rest of their own state.
